+This example assumes nginx directly receives the client's connection. If another
+proxy is in front, configure nginx real-IP handling to trust only known upstream
+proxies and to derive `$remote_addr` from their sanitized client address; otherwise
+do not use an untrusted incoming header as the client identity. Remove or overwrite
+other client-supplied forwarding headers as appropriate to the deployment. Never
+rewrite the client address to loopback.
+
+For client-IP attribution, OmniRoute automatically trusts forwarding information
+from loopback and private-network peers, as well as Cloudflare edges; additional
+proxy IPs or CIDRs can be listed in `OMNIROUTE_TRUSTED_PROXIES`. Restrict direct
+access to OmniRoute and trust only LAN clients and proxies that cannot spoof these
+headers. `OMNIROUTE_TRUST_PROXY` is a separate public-origin setting, not the
+switch for this attribution trust. A proxy with no forwarding marker is
+indistinguishable from a direct connection from its socket address.
+
 Set the allowed browser origins in OmniRoute (`CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` or the
 Security tab), not in the proxy.
 
